Z||000006||Shaun41178||02-02-2001||10:17 PM||||Chris that torque converter gave you a stall speed of 2900 rpm after you installed it in your Fiero?<P>Or was it a custom one for a Sunbird you put in your Fiero?  When you power brake it, how high can you get the rpms before the engine overpowers the brakes?<P>I can only get my tach up to about 1800 before the brakes can't hold the car motionless.  After that it begins to move through the staging lights<P>I know protorque sells a custom stall converter but that is $400.  I am sure a j-yard sunbird converter can be had for much less.  Any info would be great.  thanks<P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds<BR><A HREF="http://members.aol.com/Shaun41178" TARGET=_blank>Preferred Performance</A>||||reg||1
